      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغتبق</span></b> , (S, O, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِغْتِبَاقٌ</span>, (TA,) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغْتَبَقٌ</span> may be an inf. n. as well as a n. of place,
(O, K,) <i>He drank an evening-draught,</i> or <i>what
is termed a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَبُوق</span>. (S, O, K. [See also what
next precedes.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اغتبق لَبَنَهَا</span> <i>He drank
her</i> (a camel's) <i>milk in the evening.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
